        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://d3fend.mitre.org/ontologies/d3fend.owl#DigitalInformationBearer"/>
        <definition>A binary segment is a partition of binary information within a larger binary object, which arranges a set of binary objects for its purpose.   For example, code, data, heap, and stack segments are segments of the binary information used by a process.  Code and data segments are also found in object files.</definition>
        <rdfs:label>Binary Segment</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


