        <definition>A JAR (Java ARchive) is a package file format typically used to aggregate many Java class files and associated metadata and resources (text, images, etc.) into one file for distribution.</definition>
        <rdfs:label>Java Archive</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://dbpedia.org/page/JAR_(file_format)"/>
    </owl:Class>
    


