    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://d3fend.mitre.org/ontologies/d3fend.owl#OffensiveTactic -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://d3fend.mitre.org/ontologies/d3fend.owl#OffensiveTactic">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://d3fend.mitre.org/ontologies/d3fend.owl#Goal"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://d3fend.mitre.org/ontologies/d3fend.owl#enabled-by"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://d3fend.mitre.org/ontologies/d3fend.owl#OffensiveTechnique"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <definition>Per ATT&amp;CK, these are defined as Tactical Goals, not Tactics per se. Many children also fit definition of tactics.  Some are neither tactics or tactical goals really (e.g., Execution, which is a useful grouping, but an action, not really a tactic or technique.</definition>
        <synonym>Tactical Objective</synonym>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://attack.mitre.org/docs/ATTACK_Design_and_Philosophy_March_2020.pdf"/>
        <rdfs:label>Offensive Tactic</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://d3fend.mitre.org/ontologies/d3fend.owl#OffensiveTechnique -->

