    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://d3fend.mitre.org/ontologies/d3fend.owl#InputDevice">
        <definition>In computing, an input device is a piece of equipment used to provide data and control signals to an information processing system such as a computer or information appliance. Examples of input devices include keyboards, mouse, scanners, digital cameras, joysticks, and microphones. Input devices can be categorized based on:</definition>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Input_device"/>
