        <definition>A job scheduler software is operating system software that when run executes scheduled tasks (time-scheduling in the sense of wall clock time; not operating system scheduling of processes for multitasking). Processes running such software are task scheduler processes. In Windows, Scheduled Tasks are created and managed by the Task Scheduler. In Unix-like OSes, the `cron` utitility serves a similar role.</definition>
        <synonym>Task Scheduler Software</synonym>
        <rdfs:label>Job Scheduler Software</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://d3fend.mitre.org/ontologies/d3fend.owl#ScheduledJob"/>
